Even with the button released, the Serial monitor sometimes prints "BASILDI" (pressed). Which line is wrong?

```
void setup() {
  Serial.begin(9600);
  pinMode(2, INPUT);
}

void loop() {
  if (digitalRead(2) == LOW) {
    Serial.println("BASILDI");
  }
  delay(100);
}
```

The centre is 512. The stick is pushed slightly and the raw value is 540. What does the Serial monitor show when this code runs?

```
int merkez = 512;
int ham = 540;
int fark = ham - merkez;
if (abs(fark) < 40) {
  Serial.println("ORTA");
} else if (fark > 0) {
  Serial.println("SAG");
} else {
  Serial.println("SOL");
}
```
